1
00:00:00,785 --> 00:00:03,744
Was that it, grade One sorcerer?

2
00:00:03,827 --> 00:00:05,535
You did well running around,

3
00:00:05,618 --> 00:00:07,785
but you're at your
limit now, aren't you?

4
00:00:09,953 --> 00:00:13,161
(resigned sigh)

5
00:00:13,244 --> 00:00:14,661
Unfortunately...

6
00:00:17,244 --> 00:00:18,870
What?

7
00:00:18,953 --> 00:00:20,870
His cursed energy's increasing?

8
00:00:21,786 --> 00:00:22,828
Thanks to you.

9
00:00:23,995 --> 00:00:26,078
I'm going to have
to go into overtime.

10
00:00:27,161 --> 00:00:28,203
Overtime?

11
00:00:30,079 --> 00:00:32,079
A time-based pact!

12
00:00:32,162 --> 00:00:35,203
Was he limiting his own
cursed energy until now?

13
00:00:36,454 --> 00:00:37,620
So much fun!

14
00:00:40,245 --> 00:00:43,038
My cursed technique
draws a line along the target

15
00:00:43,120 --> 00:00:45,829
and using a ratio
of seven to three,

16
00:00:45,912 --> 00:00:48,913
then creates a weak point
at exactly that location.

17
00:00:49,455 --> 00:00:51,204
I can create this
line along more

18
00:00:51,288 --> 00:00:54,580
than just their full
height or wingspan.

19
00:00:54,663 --> 00:00:57,039
And I can designate
it along various parts,

20
00:00:57,121 --> 00:01:00,080
such as the head, upper
arm, forearm, and so on.

21
00:01:02,204 --> 00:01:04,580
This cursed technique can affect

22
00:01:04,663 --> 00:01:06,831
more than just living
creatures, as well.

23
00:01:08,205 --> 00:01:10,664
He's revealing his technique?

24
00:01:12,122 --> 00:01:13,122
You're serious huh?

25
00:01:15,873 --> 00:01:16,914
At present--

26
00:01:18,081 --> 00:01:21,040
The first way I can see to
exorcise this cursed spirit

27
00:01:21,122 --> 00:01:22,289
is to continue damaging him

28
00:01:22,372 --> 00:01:24,331
until he runs out
of cursed energy.

29
00:01:26,041 --> 00:01:28,540
However, that's not
sustainable for me.

30
00:01:30,041 --> 00:01:32,332
The second way is to
reduce him to smithereens

31
00:01:32,415 --> 00:01:33,665
with a single blow.

32
00:01:35,332 --> 00:01:36,372
Ratio Technique: Collapse!

33
00:01:38,498 --> 00:01:40,457
What power!

34
00:01:40,540 --> 00:01:42,623
And was that really
cursed energy I felt,

35
00:01:42,707 --> 00:01:43,790
racing through it!

36
00:01:43,874 --> 00:01:45,333
No way!

37
00:01:45,416 --> 00:01:47,000
It's an expanded technique

38
00:01:47,083 --> 00:01:49,791
that imbues the destroyed
target with cursed energy!

39
00:01:49,875 --> 00:01:50,666
And, it's a wide-range attack

40
00:01:50,750 --> 00:01:53,833
that probably puts
him at risk, too.

41
00:01:53,916 --> 00:01:54,499
So...

42
00:01:54,583 --> 00:01:56,916
I guess I should dodge this!

43
00:02:00,333 --> 00:02:01,750
I'm going to withdraw.

44
00:02:02,374 --> 00:02:05,500
You should get that
leg healed up quickly.

45
00:02:06,917 --> 00:02:09,792
If we're both still alive,
let's meet up again.

46
00:02:11,125 --> 00:02:12,167
Huh.

47
00:02:12,751 --> 00:02:13,792
Huh?

48
00:02:17,709 --> 00:02:21,001
(Opening Theme Music)

49
00:03:48,797 --> 00:03:49,547
"Episode 11: Narrow-minded"

50
00:03:49,630 --> 00:03:50,547
Huh?

51
00:03:50,630 --> 00:03:52,380
Did the ground just shake?

52
00:03:52,464 --> 00:03:54,297
Yeah, it did.

53
00:03:54,380 --> 00:03:56,213
Intensity Two or so?

54
00:03:56,297 --> 00:03:58,340
(phone ringing)

55
00:03:58,423 --> 00:03:59,298
Damn it!

56
00:03:59,381 --> 00:04:01,631
Ijichi's not answering!

57
00:04:03,465 --> 00:04:05,590
I probably shouldn't
even talk to you.

58
00:04:05,673 --> 00:04:06,757
Hm?

59
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:07,631
Is it really okay for me

60
00:04:07,715 --> 00:04:10,757
to be asking him
questions like this?

61
00:04:10,840 --> 00:04:13,715
How much am I allowed to
reveal about Jujutsu Tech, anyway?

62
00:04:15,465 --> 00:04:17,257
[Phone Voice] The
person you have called,

63
00:04:17,341 --> 00:04:18,591
is not available at this time.

64
00:04:18,674 --> 00:04:19,966
[Itadori] Pick up, damn it!

65
00:04:20,050 --> 00:04:22,257
(laughing chittering,
warbling sounds)

66
00:04:22,341 --> 00:04:23,483
Come back here you little curse!

67
00:04:23,507 --> 00:04:26,966
Ahh, I can't believe that guy!

68
00:04:27,050 --> 00:04:27,883
What's going on?

69
00:04:27,966 --> 00:04:29,466
[Junpei] A button
with a swirl on it.

70
00:04:29,549 --> 00:04:30,466
So.

71
00:04:30,549 --> 00:04:33,424
If you happen to meet
someone wearing a button

72
00:04:33,507 --> 00:04:36,425
with a swirl like this,
then be friendly to them.

73
00:04:36,508 --> 00:04:39,508
Because they're
jujutsu sorcerers.

74
00:04:39,592 --> 00:04:41,508
I'm sure you'll find
that you get along.

75
00:04:43,051 --> 00:04:46,258
But, the jujutsu sorcerers
are Mahito's enemies,

76
00:04:46,342 --> 00:04:47,258
aren't they?

77
00:04:47,342 --> 00:04:48,633
Aaargghh, forget it!

78
00:04:48,717 --> 00:04:49,342
I'm just going to ask!

79
00:04:49,425 --> 00:04:50,633
So then.

80
00:04:50,717 --> 00:04:54,258
You were there in the theater
the day those guys got killed.

81
00:04:54,342 --> 00:04:55,217
Huh?

82
00:04:55,301 --> 00:04:56,593
Did you happen to see anything?

83
00:04:56,676 --> 00:04:57,509
Maybe a weird
little thing like this?

84
00:04:57,593 --> 00:04:59,885
Uhh. No.

85
00:05:00,134 --> 00:05:01,676
Afraid not.

86
00:05:01,760 --> 00:05:04,176
I've just started seeing
those things recently.

87
00:05:04,718 --> 00:05:07,052
Gotcha.

88
00:05:07,134 --> 00:05:08,444
Well I've got nothing
else to ask you then!

89
00:05:08,468 --> 00:05:09,509
That was all?

90
00:05:11,259 --> 00:05:12,176
But if you don't mind

91
00:05:12,259 --> 00:05:14,011
could you wait until
the other guy shows up?

92
00:05:14,094 --> 00:05:14,635
He's kinda like my boss.

93
00:05:14,719 --> 00:05:16,677
Okay sure.

94
00:05:16,761 --> 00:05:17,761
Cool, thanks!

95
00:05:18,510 --> 00:05:21,719
So, what was showing
at that theater?

96
00:05:21,802 --> 00:05:23,969
It was a repeat
screening of an old movie.

97
00:05:24,053 --> 00:05:25,469
But I doubt you've
ever heard of it.

98
00:05:25,552 --> 00:05:27,177
Aaaah, come on, try me.

99
00:05:28,761 --> 00:05:30,177
[Junpei] Human Earthworm Three.

100
00:05:30,260 --> 00:05:31,469
That movie was super boring!

101
00:05:31,552 --> 00:05:35,054
I got punched so many
times over that one.

102
00:05:35,136 --> 00:05:36,845
You got punched?

103
00:05:36,928 --> 00:05:38,553
It was boring.

104
00:05:38,636 --> 00:05:40,428
But after all it's
just a splatter film.

105
00:05:40,511 --> 00:05:42,054
So maybe it's our own fault

106
00:05:42,136 --> 00:05:44,219
for expecting it to
deliver any more than that.

107
00:05:44,303 --> 00:05:44,678
Mm-hmm.

108
00:05:44,762 --> 00:05:46,887
But Two.

109
00:05:46,970 --> 00:05:49,219
Two was actually a
pretty good one wasn't it?

110
00:05:49,928 --> 00:05:50,845
Yeah!

111
00:05:50,928 --> 00:05:52,013
Yeah it was!

112
00:05:52,096 --> 00:05:54,220
It was the only one
you could actually enjoy!

113
00:05:54,304 --> 00:05:54,637
[Itadori] What do
you mean enjoy?

114
00:05:54,721 --> 00:05:55,721
We've got him.

115
00:05:55,804 --> 00:05:58,346
Well, you probably have
to watch the whole series

116
00:05:58,429 --> 00:05:59,572
one after the
other to really get it.

117
00:05:59,596 --> 00:06:02,096
[Junpei] At first glance,
Human Earthworm Two

118
00:06:02,179 --> 00:06:04,346
looks like it's not
going to be any different

119
00:06:04,429 --> 00:06:06,055
from One or Three.

120
00:06:06,137 --> 00:06:07,739
But, in the end, it captures
the changing emotions

121
00:06:07,763 --> 00:06:11,347
of the perfectionist who
abandons everything.

122
00:06:11,430 --> 00:06:12,847
(fright gasp)

123
00:06:12,930 --> 00:06:14,014
[Man] Mama.

124
00:06:14,680 --> 00:06:17,138
[Itadori] Ah, so that's
why I was able to get

125
00:06:17,221 --> 00:06:18,347
-through Two.
-Why, Mom?

126
00:06:19,805 --> 00:06:21,656
At first, I couldn't understand
what was so good about it.

127
00:06:21,680 --> 00:06:23,472
So I watched it
three more times.

128
00:06:23,555 --> 00:06:25,555
And that wasn't easy

129
00:06:25,638 --> 00:06:27,638
'cause the gory scenes
are pretty realistic.

130
00:06:28,805 --> 00:06:30,046
You're really serious about it.

131
00:06:32,181 --> 00:06:33,598
Do you like movies, Itadori?

132
00:06:34,681 --> 00:06:35,473
Well, I've had a reason to watch

133
00:06:35,556 --> 00:06:38,306
a lot more of them lately.

134
00:06:38,389 --> 00:06:40,639
But I haven't been going
to theaters to see them.

135
00:06:40,723 --> 00:06:41,890
Wait, why not?

136
00:06:41,973 --> 00:06:43,264
The emotional impact of seeing

137
00:06:43,348 --> 00:06:45,264
a good movie at
the theater is huge.

138
00:06:45,348 --> 00:06:47,890
Even if on-demand
ones are more convenient.

139
00:06:47,973 --> 00:06:49,783
I can't even remember
the last time I did that.

140
00:06:49,807 --> 00:06:53,265
You should take me the
next time you go to one.

141
00:06:53,349 --> 00:06:54,390
Huh?

142
00:06:55,349 --> 00:06:57,182
[Itadori] Oh, you
need my number?

143
00:06:57,265 --> 00:06:58,307
Go ahead.

144
00:07:00,390 --> 00:07:03,182
Wait, how do I
add friends again?

145
00:07:03,265 --> 00:07:04,599
[Nagi] Oh Junpei!

146
00:07:04,682 --> 00:07:05,974
there you are.

147
00:07:06,058 --> 00:07:07,182
[Junpei] Mom?

148
00:07:07,265 --> 00:07:08,546
How unusual to see you out here.

149
00:07:08,600 --> 00:07:10,808
That a friend of yours?

150
00:07:10,892 --> 00:07:11,641
Actually we just met.

151
00:07:11,725 --> 00:07:14,433
Yeah, but we have
a lot in common!

152
00:07:14,516 --> 00:07:15,659
So I think we're
gonna be good friends!

153
00:07:15,683 --> 00:07:17,683
Really?

154
00:07:17,767 --> 00:07:19,647
Well, I hope the two of
you become fast friends.

155
00:07:19,725 --> 00:07:20,641
[Junpei] Mom!

156
00:07:20,725 --> 00:07:21,767
Hm?

157
00:07:21,850 --> 00:07:23,600
We agreed...

158
00:07:24,767 --> 00:07:27,601
You promised me
you'd quit smoking.

159
00:07:27,684 --> 00:07:29,434
Oh, right, sorry.

160
00:07:29,517 --> 00:07:32,101
I did promise not to smoke
in front of you anymore.

161
00:07:34,018 --> 00:07:35,976
So what's your friend's name?

162
00:07:36,060 --> 00:07:36,893
I'm Yuuji Itadori.

163
00:07:36,976 --> 00:07:40,018
You know, you look
weird with green onions.

164
00:07:40,101 --> 00:07:41,184
Oh, you think so?

165
00:07:41,267 --> 00:07:43,726
I don't really wanna be a
green onions type of woman!

166
00:07:43,809 --> 00:07:44,889
What are you talking about?

167
00:07:44,934 --> 00:07:47,852
[Nagi] Yuuji, would you
care to join us for dinner?

168
00:07:47,935 --> 00:07:48,560
Wha-? No, mom!

169
00:07:48,643 --> 00:07:49,560
Quit bothering him!

170
00:07:49,643 --> 00:07:51,643
Oh yeah?

171
00:07:51,727 --> 00:07:52,870
Are you saying my
cooking is a bother?

172
00:07:52,894 --> 00:07:54,643
-Huh?
-Hm?

173
00:07:55,560 --> 00:07:57,393
"Rumble"

174
00:07:57,477 --> 00:07:59,019
Are there any
foods you don't like,

175
00:07:59,102 --> 00:08:00,560
or anything you're allergic to?

176
00:08:00,643 --> 00:08:01,685
[Itadori] Nope!

177
00:08:08,103 --> 00:08:11,353
("hoo boy!" whistle)

178
00:08:12,728 --> 00:08:16,644
Huh?

179
00:08:16,728 --> 00:08:19,062
(laughter)

180
00:08:20,062 --> 00:08:21,436
It turns out that sorcerer

181
00:08:21,519 --> 00:08:22,912
is a whole lot
crazier than he looks.

182
00:08:22,936 --> 00:08:26,063
The two of you
went at it quite hard.

183
00:08:26,145 --> 00:08:27,063
Getou!

184
00:08:27,145 --> 00:08:28,687
That guy was interesting.

185
00:08:28,771 --> 00:08:29,604
I learned a whole lot from him.

186
00:08:29,687 --> 00:08:31,812
Oh?

187
00:08:31,896 --> 00:08:33,812
I learned even if I'm pulverized

188
00:08:33,896 --> 00:08:36,771
I won't die as long as I
maintain my soul shape.

189
00:08:36,854 --> 00:08:41,312
Cursed energy consumption
counts toward supplementation.

190
00:08:41,395 --> 00:08:42,913
It looks like there's
really no risk to me.

191
00:08:42,937 --> 00:08:45,730
No matter how much I tweak
the shape of my own soul.

192
00:08:45,813 --> 00:08:49,521
Next time I'll let loose
and try all kinds of things.

193
00:08:49,605 --> 00:08:50,521
Getou.

194
00:08:50,605 --> 00:08:50,897
Some clothes?

195
00:08:50,980 --> 00:08:53,064
No, sorry.

196
00:08:53,146 --> 00:08:55,229
Where'd your opponent go?

197
00:08:55,313 --> 00:08:56,229
I don't know.

198
00:08:56,313 --> 00:08:58,396
He just told me he
was going to withdraw.

199
00:08:58,480 --> 00:09:00,105
But he might've gotten buried.

200
00:09:01,521 --> 00:09:02,522
What?

201
00:09:02,564 --> 00:09:04,356
You're at Junpei
Yoshino's house?

202
00:09:04,439 --> 00:09:05,065
That's a bit risky!

203
00:09:05,147 --> 00:09:07,106
[Itadori] I know, but it's fine.

204
00:09:07,189 --> 00:09:08,773
Gotta go, we're
about to have dinner.

205
00:09:08,856 --> 00:09:10,314
You're having dinner?

206
00:09:10,397 --> 00:09:12,106
I'll head over to you at once.

207
00:09:12,189 --> 00:09:15,147
If you sense trouble, get
out of there immediately.

208
00:09:15,856 --> 00:09:19,106
Even if Junpei was involved
in the theater murders,

209
00:09:19,189 --> 00:09:20,749
I doubt he's capable
of killing Itadori.

210
00:09:20,814 --> 00:09:23,273
But still, as his supervisor

211
00:09:23,357 --> 00:09:25,357
this is a huge
blunder on my part.

212
00:09:25,857 --> 00:09:30,482
I can get away with it with
Gojou, as laid-back as he is.

213
00:09:30,565 --> 00:09:32,982
But if the adult of
adults, Nanami, finds out,

214
00:09:33,066 --> 00:09:34,648
he'll chew me a new one!

215
00:09:35,815 --> 00:09:37,899
I'll probably burst into tears!

216
00:09:37,982 --> 00:09:39,231
I've got to get moving!

217
00:09:40,190 --> 00:09:41,441
You don't want to cry

218
00:09:41,524 --> 00:09:43,044
in front of others
at your age, do you?

219
00:09:43,941 --> 00:09:45,608
(phone vibrates)

220
00:09:45,691 --> 00:09:46,524
"Nanami Kento"

221
00:09:46,608 --> 00:09:48,001
Ahhh, he wasn't supposed
to call me so soon!

222
00:09:48,025 --> 00:09:50,649
He's gonna chew me out for sure!

223
00:09:51,399 --> 00:09:51,816
Hello, I'm sorry!

224
00:09:51,900 --> 00:09:54,316
Hm?

225
00:09:54,399 --> 00:09:55,858
I've just sent you my location.

226
00:09:55,941 --> 00:09:58,108
Please come and
pick me up a.s.a.p.

227
00:09:58,191 --> 00:10:00,317
I need you to take
me to Jujutsu Tech,

228
00:10:00,400 --> 00:10:01,692
to get some
treatment from Ieiri.

229
00:10:01,776 --> 00:10:04,150
[Ijichi] Treatment?

230
00:10:04,233 --> 00:10:05,525
Nothing serious.

231
00:10:05,609 --> 00:10:07,942
Nothing that's going
to kill me at least.

232
00:10:08,026 --> 00:10:09,150
That's good.

233
00:10:09,233 --> 00:10:11,150
Well, I'm about to
join up with Itadori.

234
00:10:11,233 --> 00:10:13,150
Then we'll head your way.

235
00:10:13,233 --> 00:10:14,150
[Nanami] What?

236
00:10:14,233 --> 00:10:15,525
He's not with you?

237
00:10:15,609 --> 00:10:16,525
Idiot!

238
00:10:16,609 --> 00:10:17,817
Why'd you tell him that?

239
00:10:21,027 --> 00:10:23,860
(short inhale into long sigh)

240
00:10:23,943 --> 00:10:26,110
I had to really practice a lot.

241
00:10:27,443 --> 00:10:30,193
You'll make the
perfect test subject.

242
00:10:30,276 --> 00:10:31,818
Luck's really on my side.

243
00:10:35,276 --> 00:10:38,361
That cursed spirit
is just a child.

244
00:10:38,444 --> 00:10:39,986
It probably hasn't
been that long

245
00:10:40,070 --> 00:10:42,028
since he sprang into being.

246
00:10:42,111 --> 00:10:43,861
And he's greedily
enjoying his own growth.

247
00:10:46,486 --> 00:10:49,361
The two special-grade
cursed spirits that Gojou fought

248
00:10:49,444 --> 00:10:50,986
had mastered domain expansion.

249
00:10:51,070 --> 00:10:52,861
If this one manages to survive,

250
00:10:52,944 --> 00:10:55,944
it won't be much longer
before he reaches that stage, too.

251
00:10:57,071 --> 00:10:59,195
On top of that,

252
00:10:59,278 --> 00:11:02,029
his victim count far
exceeded our predictions.

253
00:11:02,112 --> 00:11:03,278
Please, help me.

254
00:11:04,904 --> 00:11:08,862
We need to exorcise
him as soon as possible.

255
00:11:08,945 --> 00:11:10,278
Before it's too late.

256
00:11:13,945 --> 00:11:15,862
(laughter)

257
00:11:15,945 --> 00:11:18,571
[Nagi] What happened then?

258
00:11:18,654 --> 00:11:21,696
So Takashi, he's all full of
confidence and he yells...

259
00:11:21,780 --> 00:11:23,696
This is the larva
of a weird species!

260
00:11:23,780 --> 00:11:25,196
It might even be poisonous!

261
00:11:25,279 --> 00:11:26,030
Get back! Don't touch it!

262
00:11:26,113 --> 00:11:28,696
So then of course
I picked it up,

263
00:11:28,780 --> 00:11:31,237
and it turned out to be a
konjac noodle from lunch!

264
00:11:31,321 --> 00:11:33,571
(uproarious laughter)

265
00:11:33,654 --> 00:11:34,571
[Nagi] Wait, no way!

266
00:11:34,654 --> 00:11:36,238
Konjac? It was just
a konjac noodle?

267
00:11:36,322 --> 00:11:38,031
Mom, you've had
too much to drink.

268
00:11:38,114 --> 00:11:40,906
[Nagi] Oh, you are funny, Yuuji!

269
00:11:40,989 --> 00:11:44,447
She's the worst kind of drunk.

270
00:11:44,530 --> 00:11:45,697
Wilson!

271
00:11:45,781 --> 00:11:46,697
Wilson!

272
00:11:46,781 --> 00:11:48,364
Forgive me, Wilson!

273
00:11:48,447 --> 00:11:49,447
Ha ha!

274
00:11:49,489 --> 00:11:50,673
That's from Castaway, isn't it?

275
00:11:50,697 --> 00:11:51,614
That's right!

276
00:11:51,697 --> 00:11:53,614
Is that from a movie?

277
00:11:53,697 --> 00:11:54,907
I don't get it.

278
00:11:54,990 --> 00:11:56,740
It's fire!

279
00:11:56,823 --> 00:11:58,907
(laughter)

280
00:12:03,198 --> 00:12:05,948
(soft sleeping or snoring)

281
00:12:07,032 --> 00:12:09,740
Your mom's really cool.

282
00:12:09,823 --> 00:12:10,823
And nice.

283
00:12:12,074 --> 00:12:13,115
Mm-hmm.

284
00:12:15,574 --> 00:12:16,925
[Nagi] Staying home
from school again?

285
00:12:16,949 --> 00:12:19,449
(sad sigh)

286
00:12:19,532 --> 00:12:20,449
It's okay.

287
00:12:20,532 --> 00:12:21,741
You don't have to go.

288
00:12:21,824 --> 00:12:22,366
Huh?

289
00:12:22,449 --> 00:12:25,033
All you kids at your age,

290
00:12:25,116 --> 00:12:27,075
you tend to take these
things too seriously.

291
00:12:27,157 --> 00:12:31,240
If you think about it,
school is just a tiny aquarium.

292
00:12:32,075 --> 00:12:35,117
After all, there's a
whole ocean out there.

293
00:12:35,200 --> 00:12:37,117
Swim where you want to swim.

294
00:12:37,200 --> 00:12:40,117
Hey, that was a pretty
cool thing to say, wasn't it?

295
00:12:40,200 --> 00:12:42,158
What a brilliant saying!

296
00:12:42,241 --> 00:12:43,241
Way to go, me!

297
00:12:44,158 --> 00:12:46,367
(chuckle)

298
00:12:49,200 --> 00:12:49,992
So hey, tell me about your mom.

299
00:12:50,076 --> 00:12:51,868
What's she like?

300
00:12:51,951 --> 00:12:52,951
Well I...

301
00:12:52,993 --> 00:12:54,053
I never really got to know her.

302
00:12:54,077 --> 00:12:57,576
Though I do have a few
faint memories of my father.

303
00:12:58,368 --> 00:13:00,201
Fortunately, I had my grandpa.

304
00:13:01,077 --> 00:13:01,993
(phone vibrates)

305
00:13:02,077 --> 00:13:02,993
Oh!

306
00:13:03,077 --> 00:13:04,077
Gotta take this call.

307
00:13:06,159 --> 00:13:07,201
Hey there, Ijichi.

308
00:13:08,035 --> 00:13:09,035
Yeah, I'm fine.

309
00:13:10,035 --> 00:13:12,285
Actually, we were just
about to watch a movie.

310
00:13:13,619 --> 00:13:14,619
Okay.

311
00:13:16,078 --> 00:13:16,994
Two hours from now,

312
00:13:17,078 --> 00:13:18,202
-got it.
-Two hours!

313
00:13:19,452 --> 00:13:20,369
[Junpei] Itadori.

314
00:13:20,452 --> 00:13:22,535
You're a jujutsu
sorcerer, right?

315
00:13:22,619 --> 00:13:23,160
Yeah.

316
00:13:23,243 --> 00:13:25,410
Should I have said that?

317
00:13:26,911 --> 00:13:28,994
[Junpei] Have you
ever killed someone?

318
00:13:29,078 --> 00:13:30,161
Hm?

319
00:13:30,244 --> 00:13:31,995
No.

320
00:13:32,244 --> 00:13:33,995
Someday, you'll have to fight

321
00:13:34,079 --> 00:13:37,495
bad jujutsu sorcerers, right?

322
00:13:37,578 --> 00:13:38,828
What will you do then?

323
00:13:39,244 --> 00:13:43,120
If that happens, I still
won't wanna kill them.

324
00:13:43,203 --> 00:13:44,079
Why not?

325
00:13:44,161 --> 00:13:45,495
They're bad people.

326
00:13:46,453 --> 00:13:49,371
I just think, if I
killed anyone,

327
00:13:49,454 --> 00:13:50,996
the very option of killing

328
00:13:51,080 --> 00:13:52,913
would then have forced
its way into my life.

329
00:13:52,996 --> 00:13:56,621
The value of life would
become ambiguous.

330
00:13:56,704 --> 00:13:59,537
I might start taking the
people I care about for granted.

331
00:14:00,162 --> 00:14:01,162
And that scares me.

332
00:14:06,121 --> 00:14:07,872
People don't have hearts.

333
00:14:08,163 --> 00:14:10,330
That idea saved me.

334
00:14:11,955 --> 00:14:13,330
It gave me strength.

335
00:14:15,081 --> 00:14:17,081
But, if killing someone,

336
00:14:18,955 --> 00:14:20,538
would mean tainting my soul,

337
00:14:22,497 --> 00:14:24,622
(sighs)

338
00:14:24,705 --> 00:14:26,081
then I can't kill anyone.

339
00:14:28,664 --> 00:14:33,706
(gradual moaning, waking
into yawning and inhale)

340
00:14:35,164 --> 00:14:36,247
Whoa, I fell asleep.

341
00:14:36,331 --> 00:14:39,706
I guess Junpei's friend
must've gone home already.

342
00:14:40,498 --> 00:14:41,623
Look at the time!

343
00:14:41,706 --> 00:14:43,082
I need to clean up.

344
00:14:43,164 --> 00:14:44,082
Hm.

345
00:14:44,164 --> 00:14:45,247
Huh?

346
00:14:45,331 --> 00:14:46,791
What is this?

347
00:14:46,874 --> 00:14:47,916
Eww!

348
00:14:49,165 --> 00:14:50,165
A finger?

349
00:14:58,874 --> 00:15:00,083
"Jujutsu Kaisen"

350
00:15:03,207 --> 00:15:06,166
"Jujutsu Kaisen"

351
00:15:06,249 --> 00:15:09,000
"After the Satozakura
High School Incident"

352
00:15:09,084 --> 00:15:11,792
[Ijichi] After the incident
at Satozakura High School,

353
00:15:11,875 --> 00:15:14,249
we discovered the corpse of
Junpei Yoshino's mother, Nagi,

354
00:15:14,333 --> 00:15:18,291
at their home, along with an
unsealed finger from Sukuna;

355
00:15:18,375 --> 00:15:20,125
the pinky finger from
his second left arm.

356
00:15:20,208 --> 00:15:23,291
We believe Nagi
Yoshino was attacked

357
00:15:23,375 --> 00:15:26,209
by cursed spirits drawn
there by Sukuna's Finger.

358
00:15:26,292 --> 00:15:29,043
Her remains were completely
missing from the waist down.

359
00:15:29,126 --> 00:15:31,043
There were no visible

360
00:15:31,126 --> 00:15:33,043
or detectable traces
of blood found on-site.

361
00:15:33,126 --> 00:15:36,834
The victim's body was
found lying in her bedroom.

362
00:15:37,376 --> 00:15:40,501
When the blanket covering
the corpse was pulled down,

363
00:15:40,584 --> 00:15:43,418
there were only cold packs
and ice bags beneath the torso.

364
00:15:45,418 --> 00:15:48,460
You're saying I'd just get
in your way, aren't you?

365
00:15:48,543 --> 00:15:49,835
It's you that got hurt!

366
00:15:49,919 --> 00:15:51,293
Next time take me with you!

367
00:15:52,377 --> 00:15:54,210
My partner died.

368
00:15:54,293 --> 00:15:56,127
But I wasn't with him
when it happened.

369
00:15:56,210 --> 00:15:57,127
Why not?

370
00:15:57,210 --> 00:15:59,418
Well, because I'm just a child!

371
00:16:02,211 --> 00:16:05,586
You're a strong kid,
so try to help others.

372
00:16:06,961 --> 00:16:07,878
Not again!

373
00:16:07,961 --> 00:16:09,378
I have to go!

374
00:16:09,461 --> 00:16:10,461
You can't.

375
00:16:11,461 --> 00:16:12,711
As you have seen,

376
00:16:12,795 --> 00:16:14,145
this patchwork cursed
spirit we're fighting

377
00:16:14,169 --> 00:16:16,003
uses transfigured people.

378
00:16:16,419 --> 00:16:19,628
There are some people
who are beyond saving.

379
00:16:20,169 --> 00:16:22,879
If you continue with this work,

380
00:16:22,962 --> 00:16:24,754
there will come a time
when you're forced

381
00:16:24,837 --> 00:16:26,420
to kill a person yourself.

382
00:16:28,129 --> 00:16:29,462
But this is not that time.

383
00:16:30,629 --> 00:16:33,088
If that happens, I still
won't wanna kill them.

384
00:16:33,170 --> 00:16:34,379
And that scares me.

385
00:16:36,837 --> 00:16:38,253
Please understand this.

386
00:16:38,337 --> 00:16:39,504
Being a child is not a sin.

387
00:16:42,671 --> 00:16:43,713
And so for now,

388
00:16:43,797 --> 00:16:46,505
I'd like you to continue
monitoring Junpei Yoshino.

389
00:16:50,671 --> 00:16:52,254
I don't own any black clothing.

390
00:16:52,338 --> 00:16:55,254
So I opened my mom's closet

391
00:16:55,338 --> 00:16:57,880
and put on the first
thing that caught my eye.

392
00:16:59,214 --> 00:17:01,756
The smell of the morning air,

393
00:17:01,839 --> 00:17:04,631
and getting myself to
school were all familiar.

394
00:17:05,339 --> 00:17:06,339
But today...

395
00:17:07,464 --> 00:17:11,090
This is a cursed object
known as Sukuna.

396
00:17:11,172 --> 00:17:13,923
Other curses are drawn
to it like a moth to a flame.

397
00:17:14,006 --> 00:17:16,589
Yes but, what was
that doing in my house?

398
00:17:16,672 --> 00:17:18,799
There are a lot of
curse users out there

399
00:17:18,882 --> 00:17:20,215
who curse people for money.

400
00:17:20,298 --> 00:17:22,256
It was probably
done by one of them.

401
00:17:23,340 --> 00:17:24,483
If you have the money
and the connections,

402
00:17:24,507 --> 00:17:27,298
it's easy to curse
someone to death.

403
00:17:27,382 --> 00:17:30,091
Can you think of anyone?

404
00:17:30,173 --> 00:17:33,799
Anyone who might hold a
grudge against you or your mother?

405
00:17:33,882 --> 00:17:38,008
Or perhaps, someone
dark and gloomy,

406
00:17:38,092 --> 00:17:39,359
with plenty of
money and free time?

407
00:17:39,383 --> 00:17:42,591
And the certificate
of commendation,

408
00:17:42,674 --> 00:17:43,734
and prize for the finest work

409
00:17:43,758 --> 00:17:47,257
in the national book
report competition, goes to,

410
00:17:47,341 --> 00:17:48,633
Shouta Itou!

411
00:17:48,716 --> 00:17:49,633
(audience applauding)

412
00:17:49,716 --> 00:17:51,092
Yay Shouta!

413
00:17:51,174 --> 00:17:52,758
We love you Shoutah!

414
00:17:55,716 --> 00:17:58,093
Stop it, that's embarrassing!

415
00:17:59,926 --> 00:18:00,967
[Principal] Ahem.

416
00:18:01,051 --> 00:18:02,485
Well, uh, we are extremely
pleased to have a student

417
00:18:02,509 --> 00:18:04,467
from our very own school--

418
00:18:04,550 --> 00:18:06,009
What did you do that for?

419
00:18:06,093 --> 00:18:07,842
I told you to just
write whatever,

420
00:18:07,926 --> 00:18:10,592
and here you wrote some
crap that won me this prize.

421
00:18:11,592 --> 00:18:12,842
You wanna die?

422
00:18:12,926 --> 00:18:13,842
No.

423
00:18:13,926 --> 00:18:15,134
Sorry.

424
00:18:15,217 --> 00:18:17,593
And, you didn't
win shit for yourself.

425
00:18:19,094 --> 00:18:21,301
Shouta's just too cool
for school isn't he?

426
00:18:21,385 --> 00:18:22,676
Yeah, no doubt!

427
00:18:22,760 --> 00:18:24,010
You think?

428
00:18:24,094 --> 00:18:26,218
Well I'll give him props
for being rich anyway.

429
00:18:26,301 --> 00:18:27,635
Huh?

430
00:18:27,718 --> 00:18:29,468
What's that black
thing in the sky?

431
00:18:29,551 --> 00:18:31,301
[Male Student]
Whoa, that's weird.

432
00:18:33,301 --> 00:18:36,219
Emerge from
darkness blacker still.

433
00:18:36,302 --> 00:18:38,344
Purify that which is impure.

434
00:18:45,969 --> 00:18:47,386
Hey, I did it.

435
00:18:47,469 --> 00:18:49,886
Mahito, well done.

436
00:18:49,969 --> 00:18:52,386
I can't afford to leave
any residuals of me behind.

437
00:18:52,469 --> 00:18:54,762
What are the veil's effects?

438
00:18:55,345 --> 00:18:58,345
[Mahito] No one can
escape from inside.

439
00:18:58,428 --> 00:19:00,553
Some can enter from outside,

440
00:19:00,637 --> 00:19:02,261
but only those with
weak cursed energy.

441
00:19:02,345 --> 00:19:06,512
It's an unannounced
veil, in a residential area.

442
00:19:06,595 --> 00:19:09,553
So the windows will
report it right away.

443
00:19:09,637 --> 00:19:11,345
I do hope this all plays out

444
00:19:11,428 --> 00:19:12,446
the way you believe it will.

445
00:19:12,470 --> 00:19:15,221
I think it'll go just fine.

446
00:19:15,596 --> 00:19:18,721
The course of events
was already set,

447
00:19:18,805 --> 00:19:21,262
as soon as Junpei
landed Sukuna's vessel.

448
00:19:21,346 --> 00:19:24,179
I'll cause the two
of them to clash,

449
00:19:24,262 --> 00:19:27,097
and force Yuuji
Itadori into a pact,

450
00:19:27,221 --> 00:19:29,388
giving Sukuna dominance.

451
00:19:29,471 --> 00:19:33,139
I only wish Jougo was as calm
and level-headed as you are.

452
00:19:33,222 --> 00:19:35,722
But it's cute how
straightforward Jougo is.

453
00:19:35,806 --> 00:19:36,555
And are you good with this?

454
00:19:36,639 --> 00:19:40,472
That finger, was kinda precious.

455
00:19:40,555 --> 00:19:41,764
It's fine.

456
00:19:41,847 --> 00:19:44,472
Yuuji Itadori easily
absorbed the finger

457
00:19:44,555 --> 00:19:46,389
from the juvenile center.

458
00:19:46,472 --> 00:19:49,098
As for the one we
planted at Junpei's house...

459
00:19:49,180 --> 00:19:51,099
Let Jujutsu Tech find it.

460
00:19:51,181 --> 00:19:52,556
Ah.

461
00:19:52,640 --> 00:19:53,932
Another ploy?

462
00:19:54,015 --> 00:19:54,848
Of course.

463
00:19:54,932 --> 00:19:57,932
Well, have fun, I'll be
taking my leave now.

464
00:19:58,015 --> 00:19:58,932
Wait?

465
00:19:59,015 --> 00:20:00,223
You're not staying?

466
00:20:00,306 --> 00:20:01,449
You should really
hang out and watch.

467
00:20:01,473 --> 00:20:04,473
It's going to be
quite a bit of fun,

468
00:20:06,306 --> 00:20:08,598
seeing all these
foolish kids die.

469
00:20:09,598 --> 00:20:11,265
Ungh!

470
00:20:11,349 --> 00:20:11,933
What the hell?

471
00:20:12,016 --> 00:20:13,766
What's wrong with you guys?

472
00:20:13,849 --> 00:20:14,849
Get up kids!

473
00:20:14,891 --> 00:20:15,933
Are you okay?

474
00:20:16,557 --> 00:20:18,808
[Junpei] They're not dead.

475
00:20:18,891 --> 00:20:19,891
Huh?

476
00:20:21,058 --> 00:20:21,474
Yoshino?

477
00:20:21,557 --> 00:20:22,474
What's going on?

478
00:20:22,557 --> 00:20:26,432
Do you know about this?

479
00:20:26,516 --> 00:20:28,349
Do you know what happened here?

480
00:20:28,432 --> 00:20:29,475
Teacher...

481
00:20:30,892 --> 00:20:32,433
Just watch and you'll see.

482
00:20:33,517 --> 00:20:34,433
Those...

483
00:20:34,517 --> 00:20:35,725
Those scars!

484
00:20:38,850 --> 00:20:40,767
The pain I had to go through,

485
00:20:40,850 --> 00:20:42,600
you're going to feel it now.

486
00:20:42,683 --> 00:20:44,433
Yoshino?

487
00:20:47,059 --> 00:20:48,601
I have one question for you.

488
00:20:48,684 --> 00:20:53,060
Are you the one who left
that thing in my home?

489
00:20:53,143 --> 00:20:54,060
Huh?

490
00:20:54,143 --> 00:20:55,223
What are you talking about?

491
00:21:00,768 --> 00:21:02,018
What is this?

492
00:21:02,102 --> 00:21:03,393
How are you doing that?

493
00:21:04,476 --> 00:21:05,518
Wrong answer.

494
00:21:08,144 --> 00:21:10,019
What makes you think
you're in a position

495
00:21:10,103 --> 00:21:12,477
to answer my question
with your own questions?

496
00:21:12,727 --> 00:21:15,477
You are going to die.

497
00:21:15,560 --> 00:21:17,685
Whether your
answer is yes or no.

498
00:21:18,894 --> 00:21:20,811
After all, I don't
have a technique

499
00:21:20,894 --> 00:21:21,477
to see through your lies!

500
00:21:21,560 --> 00:21:23,811
And believe me,

501
00:21:23,894 --> 00:21:26,395
you've already done more
than enough to earn your fate!

502
00:21:26,728 --> 00:21:29,478
So in your final
moments at least

503
00:21:29,561 --> 00:21:33,436
-show some sincerity.
-I'm so sorry.

504
00:21:33,520 --> 00:21:35,478
And?

505
00:21:37,645 --> 00:21:40,228
Say it, you bastard!

506
00:21:42,812 --> 00:21:45,521
(horrified gasp)

507
00:21:48,979 --> 00:21:50,354
What are you doing?

508
00:21:50,437 --> 00:21:51,729
Stop, Junpei!

509
00:21:55,146 --> 00:21:57,729
Jujutsu sorcerer, back off.

510
00:22:00,646 --> 00:22:05,688
(Closing Theme Music)

511
00:23:31,026 --> 00:23:32,151
[Nobara] The layout's great,

512
00:23:32,234 --> 00:23:32,776
but a three-burner
range portends death.

513
00:23:32,859 --> 00:23:34,984
Set it ablaze, Mt. Hiei!

514
00:23:35,068 --> 00:23:36,818
Matsutake for aroma,
shimeji for flavor!

515
00:23:36,901 --> 00:23:38,110
The tones of autumn disappear

516
00:23:38,234 --> 00:23:39,735
along with the
tears of the beloved!

517
00:23:39,819 --> 00:23:41,027
Next on Jujutsu Kaisen:

518
00:23:41,111 --> 00:23:43,193
Episode Twelve, "Bloody
Autumn Leaf-viewing."

519
00:23:43,276 --> 00:23:45,402
The hunt is on for your heart.

520
00:23:45,485 --> 00:23:49,111
(upbeat instrumental music)

521
00:23:52,069 --> 00:23:54,527
"Episode 12: To You, Someday"

